	abstract = {Let G be a compact Lie group and let U and V be ﬁnite-dimensional real G-modules with V G = 0. A theorem of Marzantowicz, de Mattos and dos Santos estimates the covering dimension of the zero-set of a G-map from the unit sphere in U to V when G is an elementary elementary abelian p-group for some prime p or a torus. In this note, the classical Borsuk–Ulam theorem will be used to give a reﬁnement of their result estimating the dimension of that part of the zero-set on which an elementary abelian p-group G acts freely or a torus G acts with ﬁnite isotropy groups. The methods also provide an easy answer to a question raised in [16].},
